Subject: Test for the frame arena before taking the entry record from its top

What this does
  Test for the frame arena before taking the entry record from its top.

Why we need it
  `regvm_light_alloc`'s entry-record branch formed `rt->regvm_frames + top` and compared against `rt->regvm_chunk_end` before the arena existed, which is pointer arithmetic on null.

What it adds
  The null test comes first and returns NULL, falling back to the record path that allocates the arena.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 9d899c8..acb9d70 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -26471,8 +26471,11 @@ regvm_light_alloc(JSRuntime *rt, JSRegRun *f, JSFunctionBytecode *cb)
         /* The entry record lives on the C stack, not in the arena, so take the
            frame from the arena top. Before the first record call there is no
            arena at all; fall back to the record path, which allocates it. */
-        size_t top = (rt->regvm_frames_top + 15) & ~(size_t)15;
+        size_t top;
 
+        if (unlikely(rt->regvm_frames == NULL))
+            return NULL;
+        top = (rt->regvm_frames_top + 15) & ~(size_t)15;
         nf = (JSRegRun *)(rt->regvm_frames + top);
         if (unlikely((uint8_t *)nf + cb->regvm_light_need
                      > rt->regvm_chunk_end))
